### Documented Runtime Boundaries & Gaps

In [`docs/screenshots/CAPTURES.md`](file:///home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-billing/docs/screenshots/CAPTURES.md), the runtime boundaries are documented plainly:
- **Runs & Webhooks RPC Authorization Boundary (`authz.no-contract-procedure`):** In `services/runs/src/auth.ts` and `services/webhooks/src/auth.ts`, the contract authorizers were defined flat (`createContractAuthorizer(RunsContractV1)`) instead of nested under `{ v1: { runs: RunsContractV1 } }`. This causes oRPC requests on `/api/rpc/v1/runs/*` and `/api/rpc/v1/webhooks/*` to fail with HTTP 403 `authz.no-contract-procedure`. As application and contract code modifications are strictly reserved for the owning agent, this was preserved and captured as an authentic boundary failure. The live durable stream transition timestamps and end-to-end multi-service trace prove the underlying background orchestration.
- **Durable Streams Island:** The run console live island maintains an active stream subscription to durable streams, requiring `domcontentloaded` wait conditions during browser automation to prevent premature timeouts.
